{
  "_doc": "src/shared/mission.ts (tool 2 of Lote 1): a mission of the APP, not a PX4 mission; it is flown with the commands that already exist (takeoff, fly_to, hold, land, rtl), nothing new on the wire. `limits` are MISSION_LIMITS. `validate`: validateMission(mission, limits) -> the issue codes in order with their waypoint index (the Spanish `detail` is recorded too and must match). `scripts`: a run is created with createRun(mission); for every step, in this order, missionControl(run, control, frame, t) if `control`, missionAck(run, ack, t) if `ack`, then missionStep(run, frame, t); `send` is everything the three returned, `phase`/`i`/`reason` the run after the step. A frame `f` is [north, east, altitude up, landed] (p = [n, e, -alt], armed = !landed). Rabbit: fly_to to start + dir·min(L, v·(t − t0) + v/1.1) at the waypoint altitude, at most every 0.5 s, the last one exactly the waypoint; arrival = horizontal < 1.0 m and |altitude error| < 0.5 m; leg deadline 2·L/v + 20 s (takeoff: alt/1 + 20 s); reaching a waypoint with holdS > 0 sends one fly_to exactly to it and waits holdS; the finish is sent once and the run is `done` at once (the phase `finish` is transient). `integration`: the square SQUARE (20 m sides, 5 m, 3 m/s) on a fresh createSim(22) stepped at 0.01 s, the runner ticked every 0.05 s from t = 0 (missionControl start, then missionStep), each command applied with simCommand at once and its reply fed to missionAck; `legs` measures each leg from the tick that starts it to the tick that leaves it (length from the leg start, meanSpeed = length / duration), `samples` is [t, n, e, alt] every 1 s, `log` every command. Measured result against the acceptance targets (< 90 s, arrival < 1 m, mean speed 3 ± 0.5 m/s): see `integration.check` (done at 29.25 s, arrival error 0.91-0.94 m measured at the tick that detects it, mean speed 2.98-2.99 m/s; the arrival error is under 1 m by construction, since it is the arrival rule). The desktop port must reproduce the scripts exactly (numbers within `tolerance.command`) and the integration within `tolerance.position` (m), `tolerance.time` (s) and `tolerance.speed` (m/s).",
  "tolerance": { "command": 1e-9, "position": 0.002, "time": 0.051, "speed": 0.02 },
